<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="/images/ThePoolLab.png"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="preload" as="script" fetchPriority="low" href="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin=""/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/fd9d1056-4dbbcf07a05c3f48.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/472-6eced84fcf03e6a3.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/main-app-ce281d8555633725.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js" async=""></script><title>Dolphin Premier vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport: Which Premium Robotic Pool Cleaner Is Better in 2026? - The Pool Lab</title><meta name="description" content="Compare the Dolphin Premier and Polaris 9650iQ Sport across cleaning performance, filtration, navigation, wall climbing, ease of use, and long-term value to determine which premium robotic pool cleaner is right for your pool."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/blog/dolphin-premier-vs-polaris-9650iq-sport"/><meta property="og:title" content="Dolphin Premier vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport: Which Premium Robotic Pool Cleaner Is Better in 2026?"/><meta property="og:description" content="Compare the Dolphin Premier and Polaris 9650iQ Sport across cleaning performance, filtration, navigation, wall climbing, ease of use, and long-term value to determine which premium robotic pool cleaner is right for your pool."/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="article:published_time" content="2026-06-03"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="The Pool Lab - Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:description" content="Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/images/ThePoolLabOG.png"/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-c67a75d1b6f99dc8.js" crossorigin="" noModule=""></script></head><body class="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100"><nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light"><div class="container"><a class="navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center" href="/"><div style="width:160px;height:90px;position:relative;margin-right:10px"><img src="/images/ThePoolLab.png" alt="The Pool Lab Logo" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain"/></div><span class="d-none d-sm-inline">The Pool Lab</span></a><button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav"><span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span></button><div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav"><ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto"><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/reviews">Reviews</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/best-of">Best of</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/guides">Guides</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/about">About</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><main class="flex-grow-1"><div class="container my-5"><nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/">Home</a></li><li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">Blog</li></ol></nav><article><h1 class="mb-4">Dolphin Premier vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport: Which Premium Robotic Pool Cleaner Is Better in 2026?</h1><p class="text-muted mb-5">Posted on <!-- -->2026-06-03</p><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-8"><div><h2>Quick Verdict</h2><p>The <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong> and <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong> are two of the most capable robotic pool cleaners available for residential pools. Both deliver excellent cleaning performance, wall climbing ability, and premium ownership experiences, but they target slightly different buyers.</p><p>The <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong> stands out for filtration flexibility, strong cleaning performance, and long-term value. It is especially attractive for pools that experience changing debris conditions throughout the year.</p><p>The <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong> focuses on premium technology, advanced navigation, app connectivity, and powerful mobility. For buyers who value smart features and modern controls, it offers one of the most feature-rich experiences in the category.</p><p>If filtration flexibility and value matter most, choose the Premier. If smart features and premium controls matter most, choose the Polaris.</p><h2>At-a-Glance Comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Dolphin Premier</th><th>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Best For</td><td>Heavy debris and filtration flexibility</td><td>Premium features and app control</td></tr><tr><td>Navigation</td><td>Very Good</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Wall Climbing</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Waterline Cleaning</td><td>Very Good</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Filtration Options</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>App Control</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Ease of Use</td><td>Simple</td><td>Feature Rich</td></tr><tr><td>Value</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Good</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Cleaning Performance</h2><p>Both robots deliver excellent cleaning results in most residential pools. The Dolphin Premier emphasizes consistent coverage and effective scrubbing while offering filtration options that can be tailored to different debris conditions.</p><p>The Polaris 9650iQ Sport combines strong vacuum power with a four-wheel-drive mobility system that helps it navigate drains, slopes, and irregular surfaces. In pools with challenging layouts, Polaris often demonstrates a small advantage in movement and obstacle handling.</p><p>For routine cleaning, most owners will find both cleaners highly capable.</p><h2>Filtration and Debris Handling</h2><p>This category strongly favors the Dolphin Premier.</p><p>The Premier's interchangeable filtration system allows owners to adapt the cleaner for leaves, fine debris, or mixed conditions. This flexibility makes it particularly effective for pools located near trees or those that experience seasonal debris changes.</p><p>The Polaris 9650iQ Sport uses a large debris canister that is easy to access and maintain. It performs well with larger debris and routine cleaning but does not offer the same level of filtration customization.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong>.</p><h2>Navigation and Smart Features</h2><p>The Polaris 9650iQ Sport was designed with technology-focused buyers in mind. It includes app connectivity, programmable cleaning cycles, remote controls, and additional automation features that create a more modern ownership experience.</p><p>The Dolphin Premier relies more on traditional operation. It focuses on cleaning effectiveness rather than connected features.</p><p>If app control and scheduling flexibility are important to you, Polaris holds a clear advantage.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong>.</p><h2>Wall Climbing and Waterline Cleaning</h2><p>Both robots are excellent wall climbers. They are capable of cleaning pool walls and reaching the waterline in most residential pool environments.</p><p>The Polaris tends to spend slightly more time at the waterline and often feels more confident on complex surfaces due to its drive system. The Premier remains highly effective and will satisfy most pool owners.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong>, by a narrow margin.</p><h2>Ease of Ownership</h2><p>The Dolphin Premier is generally simpler to own. There are fewer settings to manage, and maintenance remains straightforward once owners become familiar with the filtration options.</p><p>The Polaris provides more controls and more customization opportunities. Some owners will appreciate the flexibility, while others may prefer the simpler experience offered by the Premier.</p><p>If you prefer simplicity, Dolphin has the advantage. If you enjoy technology, Polaris becomes more appealing.</p><h2>Long-Term Value</h2><p>Value is where the Dolphin Premier continues to shine. It delivers premium cleaning performance while typically costing less than the Polaris 9650iQ Sport.</p><p>The Polaris justifies its premium pricing through connected features, advanced navigation, and enhanced mobility. Whether those benefits justify the additional cost depends largely on your priorities.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong>.</p><h2>Who Should Buy the Dolphin Premier?</h2><ul><li>Pools surrounded by trees.</li><li>Owners dealing with mixed debris conditions.</li><li>Buyers focused on filtration performance.</li><li>Pool owners seeking strong value.</li><li>Those who prefer simpler operation.</li></ul><h2>Who Should Buy the Polaris 9650iQ Sport?</h2><ul><li>Technology-focused buyers.</li><li>Owners who want app control.</li><li>Pools with complex shapes and obstacles.</li><li>Users who prioritize navigation performance.</li><li>Buyers seeking a premium ownership experience.</li></ul><h2>Final Recommendation</h2><p>For most pool owners, the <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong> offers the better balance of cleaning performance, filtration flexibility, and long-term value.</p><p>The <strong>Polaris 9650iQ Sport</strong> remains an outstanding choice for buyers who want premium technology, app connectivity, and advanced navigation.</p><p>If your biggest challenge is debris, choose the Premier. If your biggest priority is premium features and automation, choose the Polaris.</p><h2>Related Resources</h2><ul><li><a href='/reviews/Dolphin-Premier'>Dolphin Premier Review</a></li><li><a href='/reviews/Polaris-9650iQ-Sport'>Polaris 9650iQ Sport Review</a></li><li><a href='/blog/polaris-vs-dolphin-robotic-pool-cleaners'>Polaris vs Dolphin</a></li><li><a href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-polaris-9650iq-sport'>Nautilus CC Plus vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport</a></li><li><a href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-dolphin-premier'>Nautilus CC Plus vs Dolphin Premier</a></li></ul><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Which cleaner is better for leaves?</h3><p>The Dolphin Premier is generally the better choice for leaf-heavy pools because of its filtration flexibility and ability to adapt to changing debris conditions.</p><h3>Does the Polaris 9650iQ Sport clean better?</h3><p>Cleaning performance is very close. Polaris offers better navigation and mobility, while the Premier offers stronger filtration options.</p><h3>Is app control worth paying extra for?</h3><p>For owners who value scheduling, remote operation, and status monitoring, app control can significantly improve the ownership experience.</p><h3>Which model provides better value?</h3><p>The Dolphin Premier generally provides better value because it delivers premium cleaning performance without requiring the premium price of the Polaris.</p><h3>Which cleaner should most pool owners choose?</h3><p>Most pool owners will be best served by the Dolphin Premier, while technology-focused buyers may prefer the Polaris 9650iQ Sport.</p></div><div class="mt-5"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/reviews">Find Your Perfect Robot</a></div></div></div></article></div></main><footer class="bg-dark text-white text-center py-3 mt-auto"><div class="container"><p class="mb-1">© <!-- -->2026<!-- --> <!-- -->The Pool Lab<!-- -->. All rights reserved.</p><small class="text-white-50">The Pool Lab<!-- --> is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</small></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin="" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0]);self.__next_f.push([2,null])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:HL[\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n2:HL[\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n0:\"$L3\"\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4:I[3728,[],\"\"]\n6:I[9928,[],\"\"]\n7:I[8326,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"308\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js\"],\"\"]\n8:I[6954,[],\"\"]\n9:I[7264,[],\"\"]\nc:I[5826,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"308\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js\"],\"\"]\nd:I[7625,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"975\",\"static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js\",\"185\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js\"],\"\"]\ne:I[6507,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/3"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"26-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"975\",\"static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js\",\"185\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js\"],\"\"]\nb:T1d83,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003ch2\u003eQuick Verdict\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e are two of the most capable robotic pool cleaners available for residential pools. Both deliver excellent cleaning performance, wall climbing ability, and premium ownership experiences, but they target slightly different buyers.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e stands out for filtration flexibility, strong cleaning performance, and long-term value. It is especially attractive for pools that experience changing debris conditions throughout the year.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e focuses on premium technology, advanced navigation, app connectivity, and powerful mobility. For buyers who value smart features and modern controls, it offers one of the most feature-rich experiences in the category.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf filtration flexibility and value matter most, choose the Premier. If smart features and premium controls matter most, choose the Polaris.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eAt-a-Glance Comparison\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eCategory\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eBest For\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eHeavy debris and filtration flexibility\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003ePremium features and app control\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eNavigation\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eVery Good\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eWall Climbing\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eWaterline Cleaning\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eVery Good\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eFiltration Options\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eGood\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eApp Control\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eEase of Use\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eSimple\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eFeature Rich\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eValue\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eGood\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2\u003eCleaning Performance\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eBoth robots deliver excellent cleaning results in most residential pools. The Dolphin Premier emphasizes consistent coverage and effective scrubbing while offering filtration options that can be tailored to different debris conditions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris 9650iQ Sport combines strong vacuum power with a four-wheel-drive mobility system that helps it navigate drains, slopes, and irregular surfaces. In pools with challenging layouts, Polaris often demonstrates a small advantage in movement and obstacle handling.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor routine cleaning, most owners will find both cleaners highly capable.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFiltration and Debris Handling\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis category strongly favors the Dolphin Premier.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Premier's interchangeable filtration system allows owners to adapt the cleaner for leaves, fine debris, or mixed conditions. This flexibility makes it particularly effective for pools located near trees or those that experience seasonal debris changes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris 9650iQ Sport uses a large debris canister that is easy to access and maintain. It performs well with larger debris and routine cleaning but does not offer the same level of filtration customization.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eNavigation and Smart Features\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris 9650iQ Sport was designed with technology-focused buyers in mind. It includes app connectivity, programmable cleaning cycles, remote controls, and additional automation features that create a more modern ownership experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Dolphin Premier relies more on traditional operation. It focuses on cleaning effectiveness rather than connected features.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf app control and scheduling flexibility are important to you, Polaris holds a clear advantage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWall Climbing and Waterline Cleaning\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eBoth robots are excellent wall climbers. They are capable of cleaning pool walls and reaching the waterline in most residential pool environments.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris tends to spend slightly more time at the waterline and often feels more confident on complex surfaces due to its drive system. The Premier remains highly effective and will satisfy most pool owners.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e, by a narrow margin.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eEase of Ownership\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Dolphin Premier is generally simpler to own. There are fewer settings to manage, and maintenance remains straightforward once owners become familiar with the filtration options.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris provides more controls and more customization opportunities. Some owners will appreciate the flexibility, while others may prefer the simpler experience offered by the Premier.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you prefer simplicity, Dolphin has the advantage. If you enjoy technology, Polaris becomes more appealing.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eLong-Term Value\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eValue is where the Dolphin Premier continues to shine. It delivers premium cleaning performance while typically costing less than the Polaris 9650iQ Sport.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Polaris justifies its premium pricing through connected features, advanced navigation, and enhanced mobility. Whether those benefits justify the additional cost depends largely on your priorities.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWho Should Buy the Dolphin Premier?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ePools surrounded by trees.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOwners dealing with mixed debris conditions.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eBuyers focused on filtration performance.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePool owners seeking strong value.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThose who prefer simpler operation.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWho Should Buy the Polaris 9650iQ Sport?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eTechnology-focused buyers.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOwners who want app control.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePools with complex shapes and obstacles.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eUsers who prioritize navigation performance.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eBuyers seeking a premium ownership experience.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFinal Recommendation\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor most pool owners, the \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e offers the better balance of cleaning performance, filtration flexibility, and long-term value.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/strong\u003e remains an outstanding choice for buyers who want premium technology, app connectivity, and advanced navigation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf your biggest challenge is debris, choose the Premier. If your biggest priority is premium features and automation, choose the Polaris.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eRelated Resources\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/reviews/Dolphin-Premier'\u003eDolphin Premier Review\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/reviews/Polaris-9650iQ-Sport'\u003ePolaris 9650iQ Sport Review\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/polaris-vs-dolphin-robotic-pool-cleaners'\u003ePolaris vs Dolphin\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-polaris-9650iq-sport'\u003eNautilus CC Plus vs Polaris 9650iQ Sport\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-dolphin-premier'\u003eNautilus CC Plus vs Dolphin Premier\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFrequently Asked Questions\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich cleaner is better for leaves?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Dolphin Premier is generally the better choice for leaf-heavy pools because of its filtration flexibility and ability to adapt to changing debris conditions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eDoes the Polaris 9650iQ Sport clean better?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eCleaning performance is very close. Polaris offers better navigation and mobility, while the Premier offers stronger filtration options.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eIs app control worth paying extra for?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor owners who value scheduling, remote operation, and status monitoring, app control can significantly improve the ownership experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich model provides better value?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Dolphin Premier generally provides better value because it delivers premium cleaning performance without requiring the premium price of the Polaris.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich cleaner should most pool owners choose?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost pool owners will be best served by the Dolphin Premier, while technology-focused buyers may prefer the Polaris 9650iQ Sport.\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3:[[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"1\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"buildId\":\"ibMnxLVRNd6eQkSmhgFst\",\"assetPrefix\":\"\",\"initialCanonicalUrl\":\"/blog/dolphin-premier-vs-polari